+### §4.0 Current card policy — draft PR and safe handoff
+
+This operator-approved policy supersedes the local-main batch/card-PR prohibitions in §4.0-H,
+§4.1, and the linked historical Git runbooks. It defines the required behavior, not a claim that
+an installed binary already implements every step. Verify the executable and current source
+before delivery; assign unsupported steps to the existing implementation owner without bypassing
+a gate or silently changing configuration.
+
+1. The leader only coordinates and supervises. Implementation, repair, build, and test execution
+   always belong to an officially assigned worker, in that worker's card worktree. There is no
+   emergency or unavailable-worker exception. Preserve any existing diff, its base, paths, and
+   evidence before handing it to that worker; do not overwrite or appropriate another writer's work.
+2. Use a fresh, short-lived card worktree from the verified configured base, with one writer and
+   the card/commit/evidence traceability carriers. Finish the required scoped local checks, then
+   open a draft PR promptly and obtain the configured Codex review for its exact current head.
+   Keep E2E, typecheck, security and other applicable functional gates. Missing or failed review
+   never counts as success; external PR code must not receive secrets.
+3. This ADK repository permits conditional auto-merge only for a non-fork, non-bot PR authored
+   by the verified connected GitHub user. Resolve that identity from the authorized connection;
+   never hard-code a maintainer login in the product. Unknown or mismatched authorship is not
+   eligible. Other-author, fork, and bot PRs must not have auto-merge enabled and require the
+   user's test confirmation and explicit approval before merge; both are required. For eligible own PRs, preserve the latest
+   head's required CI, actual Codex review, resolved findings, protection rules, and any required
+   approval by another person. PR creation alone grants no merge permission. Keep the repository
+   public and do not automatically delete branches, including for eligible own PRs. Release/deploy needs separate authorization.
+   Direct push to main remains prohibited. This policy does not authorize management-setting,
+   visibility, or protection changes. Do not change
+   branch protection, credentials, API keys, persistent app access, or cost commitments as part
+   of a documentation or review migration without the separately required approval.
+4. A safe handoff records the PR/head, scoped test evidence, review/repair owner and next action,
+   and the owned lease/resource disposition. A worker may then take the next independent card.
+   A PR is not done: confirm remote merge and the required completion evidence before closure.
+   Keep the original branch/worktree recoverable until that boundary.
+5. Only actual code or acceptance dependencies block a successor. A failed card blocks its
+   affected dependants, not the entire backlog. End active work before releasing its owned card
+   and test/resource leases through the documented lifecycle; never edit the DB or clear another
+   holder's lease to bypass a refusal. A serial slot and a test/resource slot are separate controls.
+6. Primary-main recovery requires preservation and an explicit handoff plan first. Do not switch,
+   reset, stash, or force-checkout the shared primary to make it match main. Inventory tracked,
+   untracked and relevant ignored changes and their owners, preserve them recoverably, and delegate
+   the approved recovery to its official worker. A clean dedicated main tree does not prove the
+   shared primary is safe to move.
+7. This repository's explicitly approved factory settings stay local. Shipped defaults are
+   manual with independent opt-ins for issuance, dispatch/execution, push/PR, review repair,
+   merge, and release/deploy. Preserve existing operator choices during updates. The scoped
+   own-author ADK choice above is local, not a distributed default. Web controls and
+   runtime must share effective settings; unsupported controls remain separately owned work.
+   This policy does not authorize implementing or switching to Kanban mode.
+
